                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "destination"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " category key of the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "log category key"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "configure-runtime.html#log-key"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in a playbook. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "sync"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key is optional. The value of this key can either be "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "true"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". By default, the value is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "true"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", which means Antora writes to the destination using a synchronous operation. If you set the value to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", Antora will switch to writing to the destination using an asynchronous operation. This means log messages will be written the next time the Node.js process can perform an I/O operation."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "runtime:\n  log:\n    destination:\n      file: ./antora.log\n      sync: false"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Setting the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "sync"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prevents a log event from pausing the program to complete the write. Instead, those writes are put onto a queue and performed the next time the Node.js process is idle (i.e., async), such as when it’s performing a network operation. In other words, the writes are naturally batched. (Antora ensures that any pending writes are flushed before the process exits.)"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If generating your site produces a lot of log messages, writing those messages in async mode can help Antora perform more optimally."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can combine the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "sync"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key with the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
